{"idx": 134, "arm": "delete", "metric": "da", "text": "Looking at this translation, the machine output is \"अहं संस्कृतवर्गं\" which contains only the subject pronoun \"अहं\" (I) and the object \"संस्कृतवर्गं\" (Sanskrit class), but completely omits the verb \"चलिष्यामि\" (will conduct/will run).\n\nThe absence of the verb is a critical failure: the sentence is grammatically incomplete and fails to convey the core action and future tense of the source. A reader would understand the topic involves \"I\" and \"the Sanskrit class,\" but nothing about what will be done — whether conducting, attending, teaching, or canceling it. The accusative case ending on संस्कृतवर्गं does weakly imply a transitive action is intended, so a fragment of meaning survives, but the propositional content is largely lost", "in": 165, "out": 256}
